  "reviews": [
    {
      "author": "jbw1979",
      "content": "GEORGE TOUNAS RETURNS – AN ACHILLES RETURNS REVIEW\r\n\r\nGeorge Tounas returns with his most ambitious film yet. Achilles Returns is an independent fantasy that brings Greek mythology into the modern world with imagination and enthusiasm. Taking the legendary hero and placing him in a contemporary setting, the film blends ancient myths with present-day adventure.\r\n\r\nThe film fully embraces its mythological roots, presenting gods, heroes, and legendary conflicts with genuine passion. The gods haven't gone away—they've gone underground and evolved in a world where belief is in short supply.\r\n\r\nReturning collaborators Sabrina Culver, Jannis Sky, Matteo Pasquini, Olivia Julia Bischoff, Tuan Ryu Jin, Rico Andrew Rau, Ashraf Aziz, Irina Martel, and Katianna Ley deliver solid performances. Newcomers Céline Monjoie and Manulies Pajda stand out. Monjoie brings menace to Medusa, while Pajda commands attention as Artemis.\r\n\r\nTounas continues to expand the Tounasverse, creating a world where ancient legends collide with modern events and leaving the door open for future stories.",
      "rating": 9,
      "createdAt": "2026-06-19T15:21:49Z"
    }
